<%# locals: (gateway:) -%>
<h2>Ledgers</h2>
<p>
  Use your GatherPack ledgers as the books. Each ledger is a customer; ledgers owned by a person are linked to them.
  Charges are entries <%= gateway.charge_sign == "positive" ? "above zero, payments below" : "below zero, payments above" %>.
  Payments count against the oldest charges first. Anyone on a ledger's team can open that team's ledgers, so keep
  per-member ledgers on a team only admins and treasurers belong to; the Account Status rules decide who sees each person's result.
</p>

<% unless Accounting.enabled? %>
  <p class="text-muted">Accounting is turned off: nothing is copied until it's turned on.</p>
<% end %>

<p class="mb-1">
  Which teams' ledgers:
  <%= gateway.ledger_teams.any? ? gateway.ledger_teams.map(&:identifier_name).to_sentence : "every team" %>.
</p>
<p class="mb-1">
  Tags that mean a credit:
  <%= gateway.credit_tags.any? ? gateway.credit_tags.map(&:identifier_name).to_sentence : "none" %>.
</p>
<p class="mb-1">Team for new ledgers: <%= gateway.new_ledger_team&.identifier_name || "none" %>.</p>
<%= render "accounting/records/sync_state", source: gateway %>

<% if Accounting.enabled? && Accounting::SourcePolicy.new(current_user, gateway).customers? %>
  <%= link_to "Customers", accounting_connection_customers_path(gateway), class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
<% end %>
